-- Q10108: Public Company Reporting [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 260-10-55-12, stock splits require retroactive adjustment of all share data. Pre-split incremental shares: 10,000 - (10,000 x $60/$80) = 2,500, ratio = 2,500/200,000 = 1.25%. Post-split: 20,000 - (20,000 x $30/$40) = 5,000, ratio = 5,000/400,000 = 1.25%. Proportional dilution is unchanged.
Wrong (A): While incremental shares double to 5,000, total shares also double to 400,000, so the dilution percentage remains the same.
Wrong (B): The split does not eliminate dilutive effect; the post-split exercise price and market price maintain the same ratio.
Wrong (D): Stock option terms are adjusted for splits, so incremental shares change from 2,500 to 5,000, not remain at 2,500.$EXPL$
