-- Q10131: Public Company Reporting [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 260-10-45-22, the treasury stock method assumes proceeds from exercise are used to repurchase shares at the average market price. Year 1 incremental shares: 50,000 - (50,000 x $38/$40) = 2,500. Year 2: 50,000 - (50,000 x $38/$60) = 18,333. Fewer shares are repurchased at the higher price, increasing dilution.
Wrong (B): A wider spread between market and exercise price increases dilution, not decreases it, because fewer shares can be repurchased with fixed proceeds.
Wrong (C): The exercise price staying constant does not mean dilution is unchanged; the market price directly affects shares assumed repurchased.
Wrong (D): Options become antidilutive only when the exercise price exceeds the market price, not when the market price rises above the exercise price.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 10131;

