-- Q10229: Public Company Reporting [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 260-10-45-44, dilutive impact is measured by per-share impact (numerator adjustment / incremental shares). Both series add $22,500 after-tax interest to the numerator. Series A adds 20,000 shares ($22,500/20,000 = $1.13), while Series B adds 10,000 shares ($22,500/10,000 = $2.25). Lower per-share impact means greater dilution.
Wrong (B): Fewer conversion shares means less dilution, not more, because dilutive impact depends on the per-share impact ratio, not the denominator increase alone.
Wrong (C): Although both series share the same coupon and face value, the different conversion ratios produce materially different per-share impacts.
Wrong (D): More total shares contributes to dilution, but only because the per-share impact is lower, not regardless of the numerator adjustment.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 10229;

-- Q10235: Public Company Reporting [hard/L4]
